tui-easy-wrap

Portions of this crate are derived from first-party code in the
xai-ratatui-textarea crate, part of xAI's Grok build (grok-build) project.

Original source:
  Repository: https://github.com/xai-org/grok-build
  File path:  crates/codegen/xai-ratatui-textarea/src/wrapping.rs
  Copyright:  2023-2026 xAI
  License:    Apache License, Version 2.0

Only the smallest reusable surface was lifted out:
  - RtOptions<'a>                       — ergonomic builder around textwrap::Options
  - word_wrap_line(line, opts)          — wrap one Line, preserve span styles + indents
  - word_wrap_lines_borrowed(lines, opts) — wrap an iterator of Lines, keep borrows
  - wrap_ranges / wrap_ranges_trim      — raw byte-range helpers from textwrap
  - private slice_line_spans            — internal span-aware slice helper

The `word_wrap_lines` function and `push_owned_lines` helpers in the original
were NOT taken: `word_wrap_lines` collapses to owned Line<'static> via an
internal helper defined in another module of xai-ratatui-textarea, which is
outside the wrap-only debris surface. Use `word_wrap_lines_borrowed` and
`.into_iter()` if you need an owned Vec<Line<'static>>.

